WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.508
HKDSE 2026, Paper 1, Question 11. Topic: Partial Variation & Quadratic Graph. This is the full worked solution in English.

2
00:00:11.928 --> 00:00:22.741
It is given that f(x) partly varies as x squared and is partly constant. Suppose that f(4) equals 0 and f(8) equals minus 9.

3
00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:31.060
Denote the graph of y equals f(x) by capital gamma. (a) Find the y minus intercept of capital gamma.

4
00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:41.835
(b) capital gamma cuts the x minus axis at the points U and V while capital gamma cuts the y minus axis at the point W. Find the perimeter of triangle UWV.

5
00:00:42.255 --> 00:00:46.900
Step 1. STEP 1 — write the general form.

6
00:00:47.060 --> 00:01:00.879
Key rule: Partial Variation. y equals ax squared plus b. One part varies as x squared and one part is constant, so f(x) equals ax squared plus b with b equals 3.

7
00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:08.836
"Partly varies as x squared and partly constant" means f(x) equals ax squared plus b for constants a and b.

8
00:01:09.256 --> 00:01:14.443
Step 2. STEP 2 — use the two given values.

9
00:01:14.603 --> 00:01:25.380
Key rule: Method of Elimination. 16a plus b equals 0, 64a plus b equals minus 9 tends to 48a equals minus 9.

10
00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:32.924
Subtracting the two data equations leaves 48a equals minus 9, so a equals minus 3 over 16.

11
00:01:33.084 --> 00:01:45.394
f(4) equals 0: 16a plus b equals 0 f(8) equals minus 9: 64a plus b equals minus 9. Subtracting the first from the second.

12
00:01:45.554 --> 00:01:57.678
48a equals minus 9 which gives a equals minus 3 over 16, b equals minus 16a equals 3 f(x) equals minus 3 over 16 x squared plus 3.

13
00:01:58.098 --> 00:02:02.849
Step 3. PART (a) — y-intercept.

14
00:02:03.009 --> 00:02:11.888
Set x equals 0: f(0) equals 3. The y minus intercept is 3 (point (0,3)).

15
00:02:12.308 --> 00:02:18.285
Step 4. PART (b) — find U, V, W.

16
00:02:18.445 --> 00:02:33.420
x minus intercepts: - 3 over 16 x squared plus 3 equals 0 which gives x squared equals 16 which gives x equals plus or minus 4. So U equals (minus 4,0), V equals (4,0).

17
00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:37.084
and W equals (0,3).

18
00:02:37.504 --> 00:02:42.102
Step 5. PART (b) — perimeter.

19
00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:53.016
Key rule: Distance Formula. d equals the square root of (x sub 2 minus x sub 1) squared plus (y sub 2 minus y sub 1) squared.

20
00:02:53.176 --> 00:03:02.234
UW equals WV equals the square root of 4 squared plus 3 squared equals 5, and with UV equals 8 the perimeter is 18.

21
00:03:02.394 --> 00:03:13.197
UV equals 8, UW equals WV equals the square root of 4 squared plus 3 squared equals 5 Perimeter equals 8 plus 5 plus 5 equals 18.

22
00:03:13.617 --> 00:03:21.732
So the answer is: (a) y minus intercept equals 3 (b) Perimeter of triangle UWV equals 18.

23
00:03:22.152 --> 00:03:30.995
That completes HKDSE 2026 Paper 1 Question 11. Every step shown here matches the worked solution on the page.
